## Key Architectural Decisions

| Decision | Rationale | Status | Date |
|----------|-----------|--------|------|
| Subagent-driven, not skill-driven | Deterministic flow owned by the state machine; main agent only calls tools and reads status | Active | {{DATE}} |
| 4 tools: plan / execute / simplify / review | Handlers dispatch subagents; no pipeline logic in the main agent | Active | {{DATE}} |
| JSON state persistence | Cross-session resume via fabricium `load_state` / `save_state` | Active | {{DATE}} |
| Hooks wire lifecycle | `subagent_stop` advances the chain; `pre_llm_call` surfaces status | Active | {{DATE}} |
| No simplify/review loop cap | Review-fix loops run until the reviewer passes | Active | {{DATE}} |
| Fabricium as sole dependency | `git_utils`, CLI registration, skill bundling | Active | {{DATE}} |

